From 60bd55f3935c5d828e7cdc40ddfe47f9a67abec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:35:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] core: frontend: Fire Emblem Fates: growth view on the
 unit panel; the save-read and New Game gates are the army, not the camera
 byte

Growth view (F-049): on the bottom screen's unit panel (ViewerUnitStatus, shown
by ProcGameInfo), Select (Back on a pad; Tab in the window, instead of fast
forward while the panel is shown) or a touch on the panel's Growths button
swaps the eight stat numbers for the unit's total growth percents (personal,
with an avatar's boon/bane and a child's parent average, + class; no Aptitude),
read from the tables in memory, so a randomized game shows its laid values.
The full page gets the percents in place of its numbers; the short ("Rating")
page gets a small table. Painted into the host's copy of the bottom picture
only (read_screen_scaled; the window takes the panel from the pixels while it
is shown); nothing writes guest memory. Select and the button's touch are kept
from the game only while the panel is shown. Fates and mods on its title id
(Seal of Flames), randomizer on or off.

Camera gate (goal 7): fates_rando_session::at_title and NewGameWatch read
GameConfigData +0xB, which is the map camera angle option. at_title is now "no
player army" (fates_nuzlocke::in_game); NewGameWatch fires when the mode word
changes with no army in this frame and the one before and the rest of the
options block unchanged in this frame and the one before (a battle save's load
changes the block a frame before its word). Each save read logs which way it
went. Applies after 0027.
